# Phone previews

- Prefer `npm run start:phone`, which starts local Vite and a stable HTTPS ngrok tunnel with live reload.
- Phone previews use isolated Vite 8 bundled development mode with React Fast Refresh. Keep the normal start/build/preview commands on Vite 7 and preserve their explicit CLI paths, since npm aliases share the `vite` binary name.
- The configured preview URL is `https://finless-demystify-unopened.ngrok-free.dev/`.
- The assigned hostname and secret authtoken are in Git-ignored `.env.phone.local`; never print the token or expose it through a `VITE_` environment variable.
- Use the exact configured ngrok hostname as the phone preview URL and Firebase authorized domain. Do not authorize a shared ngrok parent domain.
- Reuse the running phone preview when available. If port 5173 is occupied, check which server owns it before stopping or replacing it.
- The prior plain HTTP LAN address is `http://192.168.49.193:5173/`. Use LAN mode only when specifically requested, and verify the Mac's current LAN IP first.
